  "history": {
    "en": "Fullara is a temple town near Labhpur in the Birbhum district of West Bengal, where tradition holds that Sati's lower lip fell. Banglapedia notes that two Attahas temples are each regarded as the pitha: this one near Labhpur, and another at Dakshindihi in the Ketugram block of Bardhaman.",
    "hi": "",
    "bn": "",
    "mr": "",
    "ta": "",
    "te": "",
    "gu": ""
  },
  "story": {
    "en": "According to the Puranas, Sati, the daughter of Daksha, gave up her life in the fire of her father's sacrifice after he insulted her husband Shiva. Grieving, Shiva carried her body across the world until Vishnu's discus divided it, and each place where a part fell became a Shakti Peetha. Tradition holds that Sati's lower lip fell here.",
    "hi": "",
    "bn": "",
    "mr": "",
    "ta": "",
    "te": "",
    "gu": ""
  },
  "facts": {
    "en": [
      "Two temples, at Labhpur and at Dakshindihi, both claim the Attahas pitha.",
      "Attahas is one of the four famous pithas of the Birbhum district.",
      "Both temples have long enjoyed the patronage of local rulers and landlords."
    ],
